WEBVTT

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:03.052
Pronouns: Agreement and Case

00:00:03.432 --> 00:00:05.736
Trace the pronoun back to its noun.

00:00:06.936 --> 00:00:08.027
How to spot it

00:00:08.427 --> 00:00:10.415
Choices like it, its, they, their

00:00:10.965 --> 00:00:13.231
The noun is far back in the sentence

00:00:13.781 --> 00:00:17.888
It’s testing: whether a pronoun matches what it replaces

00:00:19.088 --> 00:00:19.854
The method

00:00:20.254 --> 00:00:23.359
Step 1: Find the noun it replaces

00:00:23.639 --> 00:00:25.830
Trace it back, even past commas.

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.440
Step 2: One or many?

00:00:28.720 --> 00:00:30.743
Organisations count as one.

00:00:31.293 --> 00:00:33.045
Step 3: Pick the match

00:00:33.325 --> 00:00:35.032
One: it, its. Many: they, their.

00:00:35.582 --> 00:00:37.358
Step 4: Check the form

00:00:37.638 --> 00:00:39.771
its vs it’s, who vs whom.

00:00:40.321 --> 00:00:41.415
In a few words

00:00:41.565 --> 00:00:44.359
Trace it. Count it. Match it.

00:00:45.559 --> 00:00:46.341
The rules

00:00:46.741 --> 00:00:48.736
Organisations take it / its

00:00:49.016 --> 00:00:52.060
Wrong: The museum changed their hours.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.992
Right: The museum changed its hours.

00:00:55.542 --> 00:00:57.204
Plurals take they / their

00:00:57.484 --> 00:01:00.017
Right: The temples lost their paint.

00:01:00.567 --> 00:01:03.089
its = belongs to it, it’s = it is

00:01:03.369 --> 00:01:05.420
Wrong: The town and it’s festival

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.882
Right: The town and its festival

00:01:08.432 --> 00:01:10.222
who = he, whom = him

00:01:10.502 --> 00:01:13.910
Right: the archaeologist whom the team credited

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:16.553
After to, for, with: me, him, them

00:01:16.833 --> 00:01:18.134
Wrong: to Priya and I

00:01:18.414 --> 00:01:19.720
Right: to Priya and me

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:21.981
Let’s try one

00:01:22.381 --> 00:01:29.655
The orchestra, founded by a group of retired teachers in 1987, will celebrate ______ fortieth anniversary

00:01:29.655 --> 00:01:32.287
next year with a series of free concerts.

00:01:32.937 --> 00:01:35.083
Skip the part between the commas.

00:01:35.633 --> 00:01:40.242
Who’s celebrating? The orchestra. One group, so it’s singular.

00:01:40.792 --> 00:01:43.564
Their is plural. It’s means it is.

00:01:43.564 --> 00:01:47.640
They’re means they are. Its is singular and shows ownership.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:48.521
Choice B.

00:01:49.721 --> 00:01:50.790
Common traps

00:01:51.190 --> 00:01:52.452
The plural decoy

00:01:52.732 --> 00:01:55.736
A plural noun nearby that isn’t the antecedent.

00:01:56.286 --> 00:01:58.278
Organisations as “they”

00:01:58.558 --> 00:02:01.546
Fine when talking. Wrong on the SAT.

00:02:02.746 --> 00:02:05.198
Pronouns: Agreement and Case

00:02:05.478 --> 00:02:08.272
Trace it. Count it. Match it.

00:02:08.822 --> 00:02:09.402
Spot it

00:02:09.602 --> 00:02:11.427
it / its / they / their in the choices

00:02:11.977 --> 00:02:12.684
Steps

00:02:12.884 --> 00:02:15.495
1. Trace the pronoun back to its noun

00:02:15.775 --> 00:02:18.090
2. Count it: one or many?

00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:21.058
3. One → it / its; many → they / their

00:02:21.338 --> 00:02:23.552
4. Check the form: its / it’s, who / whom

00:02:24.102 --> 00:02:24.826
Remember

00:02:25.026 --> 00:02:27.118
Companies, teams → it / its

00:02:27.398 --> 00:02:30.560
its = belongs to it; it’s = it is

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:32.890
who = he; whom = him

00:02:33.170 --> 00:02:35.745
After to / for / with → me, him, them

00:02:36.295 --> 00:02:36.736
Trap

00:02:36.936 --> 00:02:39.034
A plural noun planted nearby

00:02:39.784 --> 00:02:43.202
